---
// about.astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About | staring at the ceiling" description="The philosophy behind this quiet personal corner of the web.">
  <article class="max-w-2xl space-y-8">
    <header class="pb-6 border-b border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-sans font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">
        About this space
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm font-mono text-zinc-400 dark:text-zinc-500 mt-2">
        Why it exists & the principles behind it
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose max-w-none">
      <h2>The Ceiling</h2>
      <p>
        Everyone knows the posture: lying on your back, gaze fixed upward at the blank plaster, 
        watching shadows shift as thoughts wander through ideas that rarely fit neatly into conversations.
      </p>
      <p>
        This blog is a personal ledger of those moments.
      </p>

      <h2>The Principle of Unpolished Human Words</h2>
      <p>
        We live in an era where text is continuously smoothed, summarized, and sanitized by automated tools.
        Every email sounds alike. Every blog post follows the same five-part SEO template.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Here, things are different:</strong>
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Every word is written directly by human hands.</li>
        <li>Grammatical imperfections, odd cadence, and colloquialisms are preserved deliberately.</li>
        <li>No automated tools are permitted to rewrite, embellish, or smooth the prose.</li>
      </ul>

      <blockquote>
        Perfection is sterile. The irregularities in human writing are where personality actually lives.
      </blockquote>

      <h2>Format & Architecture</h2>
      <p>
        This site is statically generated, hosted on GitHub Pages, and designed with a nod to minimalist technical documentation—fast, high-contrast, and respectful of your attention.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
